---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import Prose from '../components/Prose.astro';
import { href } from '../lib/paths';
import { APP, PUBLISHER } from '../lib/site';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Privacy Policy — HelloNotes"
  description="HelloNotes collects nothing: no account, no analytics, no tracking, no servers. Your notes are plain files on your own Mac."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
  intro="Last updated: 2026"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-[1120px] px-6 py-12">
    <Prose>
      <p>
        {APP.name} is a <strong>local-first</strong> application published by
        {PUBLISHER.legalName}. Your notes are stored as plain files on your own device, in a folder
        you select.
        <strong>
          We do not collect, transmit, sell, or have access to your notes or any personal data.
        </strong>
      </p>

      <blockquote>
        <p>
          <strong>In short:</strong> no account, no analytics, no tracking, no servers. Your data
          never leaves your Mac unless you explicitly choose to sync it somewhere yourself.
        </p>
      </blockquote>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        Nothing. {APP.name} has no analytics, no telemetry, no advertising identifiers, and no user
        accounts. We do not operate any server that receives your data. Because we hold no data
        about you, there is nothing for us to disclose, share, or delete on request.
      </p>

      <h2>Your notes</h2>
      <p>
        Your notes are ordinary Markdown files in a folder on your device that you choose. They
        remain under your control and can be read or edited by any other application. {APP.name}
        reads and writes only the folders you explicitly open, using macOS security-scoped access.
      </p>

      <h2>On-device intelligence</h2>
      <p>
        The optional Summarise, Suggest Tags/Links, Expand and “Ask your library” features use
        Apple’s on-device Foundation Models framework. Your note content is processed locally on
        your Mac and is <strong>not</strong> sent to us or to any third party. These features appear
        only on hardware where Apple Intelligence is available.
      </p>

      <h2>Optional cloud AI providers</h2>
      <p>
        {APP.name} can optionally use a third-party AI provider (such as Anthropic, OpenAI or
        Google) if — and only if — you choose to configure one with <em>your own</em> API key.
        These providers are switched off until you set one up.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you use such a provider, the text you submit for that action (for example the note
        being summarised, or your question along with relevant excerpts from your notes) is sent to
        that provider under your own account and their privacy policy. Your key is stored in the
        macOS Keychain and is never transmitted to us. The Assistant’s optional web search and fetch
        tools likewise contact the internet only when you invoke them.
      </p>

      <h2>Cloud storage and version control</h2>
      <p>
        If you keep a collection in iCloud Drive, Dropbox, Box, OneDrive or Google Drive, or connect
        one of those accounts directly, your files are handled by that service under its own privacy
        policy — the same as any other folder on your Mac. Similarly, if you use the built-in Git
        features with your own remote repository, your notes are sent only to the destination
        <em>you</em> configure. {APP.name} is not that destination and does not receive a copy.
      </p>

      <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
      <p>{APP.name} does not collect data from anyone, including children, and is rated 4+.</p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted on this page with a revised date.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${PUBLISHER.email}`}>{PUBLISHER.email}</a>,
        or see the <a href={href('/support')}>support page</a>.
      </p>
    </Prose>
  </div>
</PageLayout>
